The attached image illustrates the difference in residual local inflammation two weeks after injection of aluminum hydroxide adjuvant (AH) versus Nano-11. The left panel, representing AH, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation (indicated by asterisks) with large aggregates of inflammatory cells infiltrating the skeletal muscle (M). Conversely, the right panel, representing Nano-11, demonstrates considerably less inflammation, with only a few macrophages arranged in slender cords within the connective tissue between muscle fibers (M). This visual comparison supports the PDF's conclusion that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response that resolves more quickly than the persistent inflammation caused by aluminum hydroxide adjuvant.